<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kondavidu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kondavidu is a hill fort in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guntur">Guntur</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the 14th century it became the capital of the Reddi Kingdom, whose kings ruled coastal Andhra from it until Vijayanagara forces took it around 1424. It later changed hands between the Gajapatis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, Vijayanagara under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a>, who captured it in 1515, and the Golconda Sultanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kondavidu.jpg" alt="Kondavidu" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R., William (fl. 1784-1816) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kondavid-drug._Signed_%27W.R.%27.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
